Z||000002||1FST2M6||11-12-2001||10:04 AM||||gas tank.. same as our.. radiator.. also same as ours times 2... the radiators retail for $1235 each from modine...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>"The new 360 Modena marks another important step forward in technological and formal terms. The car’s two radiators are positioned ahead of the front wheels"<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fst360r.jpg">  <BR> <BR> <A HREF="http://fcars.4t.com/cgi-bin/i/360/___Modena%5B17%5D.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://fcars.4t.com/cgi-bin/i/360/___Modena%5B17%5D.jpg</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||11-12-2001||09:42 PM||||Pair of front radiators, directly behind the two big front openings.  Gas tank... if you can change one on a Fiero, you can change one on a 360  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000004||filthyscarecrow||11-13-2001||12:15 AM||||don't they have a pair in front of the rear wheels too where those openings are? i know there was some sort of grilled apparatus there when we saw them last year at indy. maybe they were oil coolers... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pontiaddict||11-13-2001||01:17 AM||||I thought it was a radiator on one side and an oil cooler on the other. It's possible that I'm thinking of a Porsche though.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||11-13-2001||05:51 AM||||Driver's side is engine air intake, passenger's side is transmission and crankcase pil cooler (if I remenber correctly  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The cool polished container thingie in the Vee of the motor is the engine oil sump (dry system)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
